{"term":"radiate","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:c3f7da5af7a2160276","definition":"To extend, be sent or spread out from a center like radii.","example":"Crewe North Motive Power Depot is to be modernised completely. This includes the provision of a new coaling plant, ash handling plant, and two new locomotive sheds of the latest roundhouse type, each with 32 roads radiating from a 70-ft. dia. turntable.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["corradiate","radiator","reradiate","x-radiate","eradiate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radiate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2bb4ca0bed621169e5","definition":"To emit rays or waves.","example":"The stove radiates heat.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["corradiate","radiator","reradiate","x-radiate","eradiate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radiate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6d23900a603fcde8e3","definition":"To come out or proceed in rays or waves.","example":"The heat radiates from a stove.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["corradiate","radiator","reradiate","x-radiate","eradiate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/radiate#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d8a67759db13d9c757","definition":"To illuminate.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["corradiate","radiator","reradiate","x-radiate","eradiate"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"En